    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey im working on this stripe integration and keep getting a 402 error back in the json for some reason. the card i'm using is definitely valid and has funds. what are some common reasons i'd get a 402 and how do i check if my payload is the issue?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A 402 Payment Required error in Stripe often relates to issues with your payload, especially with how you're authenticating and framing your payment. Common reasons for a 402 error could include:\n\n1. Missing 'stripeToken' in your request.\n2. Using incorrect or outdated request methods.\n3. Incorrect API versions in your request headers or body.\n\nTo debug further, verify the following elements:\n\n1. Ensure your payload includes a valid 'stripeToken' obtained through Stripe.js or Visa.me.\n2. Check if you are using the correct API version and request method (e.g., using 'POST' instead of 'GET').\n3. Validate your API key's scope and permissions.\n\nAdditionally, inspect the logs or return errors provided by Stripe beforehand to see if there's clearer feedback. You might also want to check Stripe documentation for updates regarding best practices.",
