    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. i checked the headers and they seem fine, and the stripeToken is definitely being passed in the body. i even tried with a few different test cards from their docs but i keep getting the same 402. is there any way to see the specific sub-code or error message within the stripe response that explains *why* the payment was rejected? like how do i pull the detailed error object from the response?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To retrieve a detailed error object from Stripe's response, you should check the errorParam in your HTTP request's error response. Stripe typically includes a full JSON error object with additional details when you encounter a payment failure. You can access it by inspecting the body of the response as well since HTTP responses usually contain detailed error information.\n\nFor example, using cURL, you might see something like this in the browser's developer tools or in a terminal where you run your cURL commands:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"type\": \"RESPONSE\",\n  \"reason\": \"PAYMENT_REQUEST\",\n  \"data\": {\n    \"error\": {\n      \"code\": 402,\n      \"message\": \"Missing required parameter 'stripe-token'\",\n      \"param\": \"stripe-token\",\n      \"help_url\": \"https://stripe.com/docs/solutions/stripe-on-the-web/enhanced-web-migration-centre/plan-migration/#checking-token-mismatch\"\n    }\n  }\n}\n```\n\nIn this example, you would see that the `param` is missing the required 'stripeToken' in the headers or request body, which would explain why the payment was rejected.\n\nThe `code`, `message`, and `help_url` parts of errors are very",
      "source": "target",
